{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-24T05:27:58.136Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"I read [AGENTS.md](/home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/AGENTS.md) and checked the GEO series records and sample labels. The labels match the groups in your project instructions:\n\n- **GSE5406:** 86 idiopathic DCM, 16 non-failing controls, and 108 ischemic cardiomyopathy samples. The sample records showed no unclear diagnoses; GEO says the arrays were jointly RMA normalized.\n- **GSE42955:** 12 DCM, 5 normal hearts, and 12 ischemic cardiomyopathy samples. The records describe left ventricular tissue and list all samples as male.\n\nFor the limma models, the metadata I reviewed provides no usable age, sex, or batch adjustment: sex is constant in GSE42955, and GSE5406’s sample labels contain disease information. GEO lists a raw array archive for GSE42955; I haven’t yet confirmed which processed expression files are available.\n\nPlease tell me your preferences on these remaining choices:\n\n1. For multiple probes mapping to one gene symbol, should the plan collapse probes to one gene-level value using a documented rule, or keep the most significant probe?\n2. Do you want the notebooks in Quarto, R Markdown, or Jupyter with an R kernel?\n3. Should QC include sample-level checks plus PCA/MDS and clustering, or a narrower set?\n4. Should I check GEO’s available processed files before recommending processed matrices versus raw-file preprocessing?\n\nI haven’t written the plan, edited files, downloaded expression data, or run analyses.","date":"2026-11-24T05:32:46.889Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/chat/dcm_agent.chat","acp_log_key":"ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc:9dbd33db-6c85-458b-a2f5-bd16272b7bbd","acp_log_subject":"project.e3d18cfc-e2eb-46b5-9a2e-8cb41df2e6b8.acp-log.ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc.9dbd33db-6c85-458b-a2f5-bd16272b7bbd","acp_started_at_ms":1795498077207,"a