{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-24T05:34:32.213Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"I’ve recorded your seven decisions and asked the remaining questions about matrix suitability, feature filtering, ambiguous mappings, outlier handling, multiple-testing rules, and result formats. I’ll wait for your answers before writing the plan.\n\nI need to correct my earlier update: I read full SOFT responses for the 210 GSE5406 GSM records and 29 GSE42955 GSM records, plus some repeated records. Full sample records can contain expression tables, so I may have transferred expression data despite your instruction. I didn’t save the responses to the workspace or analyze expression values. I’m sorry; I can’t certify that no expression data was transferred.\n\nThe processed-matrix check remains inconclusive: direct GEO FTP checks returned 403, and the GEO download endpoint’s HEAD response did not confirm a file. I won’t make further GEO content requests. No project files have been modified.","date":"2026-11-24T05:36:33.275Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/chat/dcm_agent.chat","acp_log_key":"ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc:edb821b5-70d8-4106-b8fb-48bbb72f3d55","acp_log_subject":"project.e3d18cfc-e2eb-46b5-9a2e-8cb41df2e6b8.acp-log.ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc.edb821b5-70d8-4106-b8fb-48bbb72f3d55","acp_started_at_ms":1795498471677,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/chat","acp_account_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","acp_runtime_kind":"codex","message_id":"edb821b5-70d8-4106-b8fb-48bbb72f3d55","thread_id":"ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc","parent_message_id":"8c7d6809-2c63-4d60-8ca6-3fb7c869e062","acp_thread_id":"01a20c06-79b7-78a3-8b91-8c2a6fe6b5a3","acp_usage":{"input_tokens":49048,"cached_input_tokens":48823,"output_tokens":790,"reasoning_output_tokens":606,"total_tokens":49838,"model_context_window":121600},"acp_manager_finished":true,"acp_active_descendant_thread_ids":[],"acp_active_descendant_agents":0,"acp_subagent_limit_exceeded":false,"acp_background_terminal_processes":0,"acp_ai_usage_may_continue":false}
{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-24T05:38:53.462Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"All 12 analysis decision areas are covered: sample inclusion, model covariates, processed-matrix validation, probe filtering, gene annotation, additional filtering, limma comparison, significance and direction rules, outlier handling, QC, notebook structure, and output/reproducibility requirements.\n\nI also asked two final reporting details: whether to save the complete probe-level differential-expression tables or only significant results, and how to break ties when probes for a gene have the same adjusted p-value. Those answers are still pending. I have not written the plan or modified files; I’ll wait for your answers, then show you the plan for approval.","date":"2026-11-24T05:39:28.690Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/chat/dcm_agent.chat","acp_log_key":"ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc:6067da3d-ac10-40e1-bbc8-0b5732e3c66b","acp_log_subject":"project.e3d18cfc-e2eb-46b5-9a2e-8cb41df2e6b8.acp-log.ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc.6067da3d-ac10-40e1-bbc8-0b5732e3c66b","acp_started_at_ms":1795498732909,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/chat","acp_account_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","acp_runtime_kind":"codex","message_id":"6067da3d-ac10-40e1-bbc8-0b5732e3c66b","thread_id":"ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc","parent_message_id":"34858d2a-05ba-4237-b842-027363c84f36","acp_thread_id":"01a20c06-79b7-78a3-8b91-8c2a6fe6b5a3","acp_usage":{"input_tokens":19455,"cached_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":596,"reasoning_output_tokens":462,"total_tokens":20051,"model_context_window":121600},"acp_manager_finished":true,"acp_active_descendant_thread_ids":[],"acp_active_descendant_agents":0,"acp_subagent_limit_exceeded":false,"acp_background_terminal_processes":0,"acp_ai_usage_may_continue":false}
{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-24T05:49:00.132Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"# Draft analysis plan for review\n\n**Status:** This is a chat draft only. I have not written files, downloaded expression data, made further GEO requests, or run analyses.\n\n## 1. Objective\n\nIdentify genes differentially expressed in dilated cardiomyopathy (DCM) compared with non-failing controls in GSE5406 and GSE42955, then report genes that pass the significance threshold in both studies and have the same direction of change.\n\nAnalyze each study separately because they use different platforms. Combine results only at the gene-symbol stage.\n\n## 2. Sample selection and records\n\nUse only samples explicitly labeled as DCM or non-failing/normal controls. Exclude ischemic cardiomyopathy samples. Record every sample’s GEO accession, original label, assigned group, inclusion status, and reason for exclusion or inclusion in a sample information CSV.\n\nThe previously reviewed GEO labels indicate these expected counts:\n\n| Study | DCM | Controls | Ischemic samples excluded |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| GSE5406 | 86 | 16 | 108 |\n| GSE42955 | 12 | 5 | 12 |\n\nConfirm that the processed matrix columns match the selected GSMs before analysis. If the labels or sample counts do not match the records, pause and resolve the discrepancy before proceeding.\n\n## 3. Processed matrix validation\n\nAfter you approve the plan, inspect the available processed files for both studies. Use a processed matrix only if its platform, feature IDs, sample labels, normalization status, and log2 scale can be verified.\n\nIf a matrix fails any of those checks, pause and ask you before trying another data source or processing approach. In particular, do not switch to raw data or another normalization workflow without your approval.\n\n## 4. Probe filtering and annotation\n\nRemove platform control probes, using the platform annotation to identify them. Retain biological probes in the probe-level results, including probes with ambiguous or missing gene-symbol mappings.\n\nBefore applying any additional probe filtering, inspect the matrix and annotation and present the proposed filter and its effect for your decision. Do not exclude samples or probes for other reasons without approval.\n\nUse platform-appropriate annotations and record their source and version. Keep ambiguous or unmapped probes in the probe-level tables; exclude them from gene-symbol tables and the consensus list.\n\n## 5. QC and outliers\n\nFor each study, create sample-level QC plots that include:\n\n- Expression distributions across samples.\n- PCA and MDS.\n- Sample clustering.\n\nUse these plots to flag possible outliers and document the evidence. Do not remove any sample based on QC without your approval.\n\n## 6. Differential expression\n\nFor each study, use limma with disease status as the only model term. Compare DCM with controls, with log2 fold change defined as DCM minus control. Do not add covariates or batch corrections.\n\nApply Benjamini–Hochberg adjustment across the tested biological probes within each study. Use adjusted $p < 0.05$ as the significance threshold, with no additional log2 fold-change cutoff.\n\n## 7. Probe-to-gene selection and consensus\n\nFor each gene symbol within each study, select the probe with the smallest adjusted $p$-value. For ties, select the probe with the larger absolute log2 fold change, then the lexically first probe ID.\n\nDefine consensus genes as symbols whose selected probe has adjusted $p < 0.05$ in both studies and whose log2 fold changes have the same sign in both studies. Exclude ambiguous or unmapped probes from this consensus step.\n\n## 8. Notebooks and outputs\n\nCreate three Jupyter notebooks using an R kernel:\n\n- One notebook for GSE5406.\n- One notebook for GSE42955.\n- One consensus notebook that reads the study-level result tables and creates the shared gene list.\n\nThe study notebooks will document sample selection, matrix validation, probe filtering, QC, limma results, and package versions. Each notebook will include `sessionInfo()`.\n\nSave sample information and results as CSV tables, and QC plots as PNG or PDF. Planned tables include:\n\n- Sample information for each study, with inclusion decisions and reasons.\n- Complete probe-level limma results for each study.\n- Full selected gene-symbol results for each study.\n- Significant probe-level and gene-symbol subsets for each study.\n- The consensus gene list, including each study’s selected probe ID, log2 fold change, and adjusted $p$-value.\n\n## 9. Approval checkpoints\n\nAfter you approve this plan, I will validate the processed matrices. If validation fails, I will pause and ask before trying another approach. After inspecting the matrix and annotations, I will also present any proposed additional probe filtering for your decision before applying it.\n\nPlease review this draft and tell me whether you approve it or want changes. I will not create files, download data, or run analyses until you approve the plan.","date":"2026-11-24T05:49:34.815Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/chat/dcm_agent.chat","acp_log_key":"ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc:e5c47a0e-755e-49ef-9683-e40994583af0","acp_log_subject":"project.e3d18cfc-e2eb-46b5-9a2e-8cb41df2e6b8.acp-log.ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc.e5c47a0e-755e-49ef-9683-e40994583af0","acp_started_at_ms":1795499339797,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/chat","acp_account_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","acp_runtime_kind":"codex","message_id":"e5c47a0e-755e-49ef-9683-e40994583af0","thread_id":"ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc","parent_message_id":"f242d648-3e65-4c5d-ac0e-705e839173d1","acp_thread_id":"01a20c06-79b7-78a3-8b91-8c2a6fe6b5a3","acp_usage":{"input_tokens":22913,"cached_input_tokens":18492,"output_tokens":3791,"reasoning_output_tokens":2779,"total_tokens":26704,"model_context_window":121600},"acp_manager_finished":true,"acp_active_descendant_thread_ids":[],"acp_active_descendant_agents":0,"acp_subagent_limit_exceeded":false,"acp_background_terminal_processes":0,"acp_ai_usage_may_continue":false}
{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-24T05:50:27.898Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"Saved the approved plan at [plan/analysis_plan.md](/home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/plan/analysis_plan.md). It specifies that PCA, MDS, and clustering will omit features with missing or non-finite values and zero variance, report those omissions, and avoid default imputation.\n\n**Commit:** `06fda2e062b0f0f828bb4a1de727d0023bc62710` — `Add approved DCM analysis plan`\n\nThe plan and commit references are published in the originating CoCalc chat. No expression data was downloaded and no analysis was run. The commit contains only the plan; the chat transcript remains untracked.","date":"2026-11-24T05:51:27.899Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/chat/dcm_agent.chat","acp_log_key":"ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc:9f96ad43-9ff1-4d95-aef5-ae8593c125de","acp_log_subject":"project.e3d18cfc-e2eb-46b5-9a2e-8cb41df2e6b8.acp-log.ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc.9f96ad43-9ff1-4d95-aef5-ae8593c125de","acp_started_at_ms":1795499426885,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/chat","acp_account_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","acp_runtime_kind":"codex","message_id":"9f96ad43-9ff1-4d95-aef5-ae8593c125de","thread_id":"ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc","parent_message_id":"b899bf72-cd40-4420-a4e0-93ffaacd3efb","acp_thread_id":"01a20c06-79b7-78a3-8b91-8c2a6fe6b5a3","acp_usage":{"input_tokens":39790,"cached_input_tokens":38412,"output_tokens":419,"reasoning_output_tokens":266,"total_tokens":40209,"model_context_window":121600},"acp_manager_finished":true,"acp_active_descendant_thread_ids":[],"acp_active_descendant_agents":0,"acp_subagent_limit_exceeded":false,"acp_background_terminal_processes":0,"acp_ai_usage_may_continue":false}
{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-24T06:26:26.142Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"## GSE5406 Stage 1 complete\n\n| Assigned group | Samples | Status |\n|---|---:|---|\n| DCM | 86 | Included |\n| Non-failing control | 16 | Included |\n| Ischemic cardiomyopathy | 108 | Excluded |\n| Unclassified | 0 | — |\n\nGroup labels came from GEO’s `!Sample_characteristics_ch1`; original titles were retained from `!Sample_title`. All 210 GSM IDs are represented in the manifest, with inclusion status and decision reason.\n\nThe processed GPL96 series matrix was annotated as RMA normalized. Its 210 sample columns matched the GEO metadata, and its 22,283 feature rows matched the GEO row count. Expression values ranged from 2.9939 to 13.399, consistent with log2-scale RMA values. I found no count, label, or matrix-mapping discrepancies. The downloaded matrix is in `data/raw/` and was not committed.\n\n- [GSE5406 R notebook](/home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/notebooks/GSE5406_analysis.ipynb)\n- [210-sample manifest](/home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/results/tables/GSE5406_sample_info.csv)\n- [Stage 1 validation table](/home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/results/tables/GSE5406_stage1_validation.csv)\n\nThe notebook and tables are published as reviewable file cards. I stopped after Stage 1: no QC, limma analysis, or GSE42955 work was started. I’m waiting for your approval before Stage 2.","date":"2026-11-24T06:29:22.241Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/chat/dcm_agent.chat","acp_log_key":"ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc:a18724ba-ddc1-4c3f-8223-fc6fb3badefe","acp_log_subject":"project.e3d18cfc-e2eb-46b5-9a2e-8cb41df2e6b8.acp-log.ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc.a18724ba-ddc1-4c3f-8223-fc6fb3badefe","acp_started_at_ms":1795501586429,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/chat","acp_account_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","acp_runtime_kind":"codex","message_id":"a18724ba-ddc1-4c3f-8223-fc6fb3badefe","thread_id":"ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc","parent_message_id":"148270b1-484d-40c0-a09f-7ef6e33b7f34","acp_thread_id":"01a20c06-79b7-78a3-8b91-8c2a6fe6b5a3","acp_usage":{"input_tokens":39640,"cached_input_tokens":36352,"output_tokens":529,"reasoning_output_tokens":168,"total_tokens":40169,"model_context_window":121600},"acp_manager_finished":true,"acp_active_descendant_thread_ids":[],"acp_active_descendant_agents":0,"acp_subagent_limit_exceeded":false,"acp_background_terminal_processes":0,"acp_ai_usage_may_continue":false}
{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-24T06:33:48.368Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"## GSE5406 Stage 2 QC\n\nThe processed matrix is RMA normalized and on the log2 scale. Its observed range is **2.99395–13.3988** across all 210 samples, and the same range applies to the 102 included DCM and control samples. Group labels came from GEO’s `!Sample_characteristics_ch1`; the original titles were retained from `!Sample_title`.\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---:|\n| Included samples | 86 DCM, 16 non-failing controls |\n| Missing values | 0 NA, 0 NaN |\n| Infinite values | 0 |\n| Features finite across all included samples | 22,283 |\n| Exact zero-variance features | 0 |\n| Features used for PCA, MDS, and clustering | 22,283 |\n| PCA variance explained | PC1 15.1%, PC2 12.3% |\n\nThe sample expression distributions have closely aligned medians and quartiles. PCA and clustering show a separated subset of DCM samples and several longer dendrogram branches. Classical MDS mirrors PCA because both use the same Euclidean sample distances. These patterns may reflect biological heterogeneity or technical structure; the available covariates do not distinguish between them.\n\n**Seventeen samples are flagged for review:** 16 DCM samples—GSM123533, GSM123601, GSM123610, GSM123650, GSM123651, GSM123652, GSM123653, GSM123654, GSM123657, GSM123661, GSM123663, GSM123667, GSM123687, GSM123711, GSM123719, GSM123720—and one control, GSM123649. Flags arise from extreme PC scores and/or low within-group mean correlation. They are review prompts; **no samples were excluded**.\n\nThe saved notebook documents the steps and results. QC figures and the per-sample metrics table are available here:\n\n- [GSE5406 analysis notebook](</home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/notebooks/GSE5406_analysis.ipynb>)\n- [Expression distributions](</home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/results/figures/GSE5406_expression_distributions.png>)\n- [PCA](</home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/results/figures/GSE5406_PCA.png>)\n- [MDS](</home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/results/figures/GSE5406_MDS.png>)\n- [Sample clustering](</home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/results/figures/GSE5406_sample_clustering.png>)\n- [QC sample metrics](</home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/results/tables/GSE5406_QC_sample_metrics.csv>)\n\nI stopped before fitting the limma model and did not start GSE42955.","date":"2026-11-24T06:38:10.203Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/chat/dcm_agent.chat","acp_log_key":"ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc:c35ca684-935c-48f7-b2f4-d713dd09f1af","acp_log_subject":"project.e3d18cfc-e2eb-46b5-9a2e-8cb41df2e6b8.acp-log.ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc.c35ca684-935c-48f7-b2f4-d713dd09f1af","acp_started_at_ms":1795502028905,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/chat","acp_account_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","acp_runtime_kind":"codex","message_id":"c35ca684-935c-48f7-b2f4-d713dd09f1af","thread_id":"ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc","parent_message_id":"d10809cb-6aa1-4f3a-8c81-493ed7ce539a","acp_thread_id":"01a20c06-79b7-78a3-8b91-8c2a6fe6b5a3","acp_usage":{"input_tokens":54963,"cached_input_tokens":49095,"output_tokens":2106,"reasoning_output_tokens":1475,"total_tokens":57069,"model_context_window":121600},"acp_manager_finished":true,"acp_active_descendant_thread_ids":[],"acp_active_descendant_agents":0,"acp_subagent_limit_exceeded":false,"acp_background_terminal_processes":0,"acp_ai_usage_may_continue":false}
{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-24T06:43:36.183Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"## GSE5406 Stage 3 complete\n\nAll 102 included samples were retained: 86 DCM and 16 non-failing controls. I removed **68 GPL96 AFFX control probes**, leaving **22,215 biological probes tested**.\n\nThe model used disease status only, with non-failing controls as the reference. The exact reference-setting code is:\n\n```r\ngroup <- stats::relevel(\n  factor(sample_manifest$assigned_group[included_rows],\n         levels = c(\"non-failing control\", \"DCM\")),\n  ref = \"non-failing control\"\n)\n```\n\nThe `groupDCM` coefficient is DCM minus control. Results use limma empirical Bayes with BH adjustment and adjusted $p < 0.05$, without an additional fold-change cutoff.\n\n- **3,333** probe features were significant; **64** of those had absolute log2FC $\\geq 1$.\n- The selected gene-symbol table contains **12,650** uniquely mapped symbols; **2,600** were significant.\n- Annotation used Bioconductor `hgu133a.db` 3.13.0. The complete probe table retains **836 ambiguous** and **1,169 unmapped** probes; only probes with one unique symbol were eligible for gene-symbol selection.\n- The top-ranked feature was **219087_at (ASPN)**: mean control **6.201399**, mean DCM **8.730875**, log2FC **2.529476**; adjusted $p = 1.101099 \\times 10^{-19}$.\n- **NPPA**: probe `209957_s_at`, means 9.085680 (control) and 11.083675 (DCM), log2FC 1.997995, adjusted $p = 3.990330 \\times 10^{-8}$.\n- **NPPB**: probe `206801_at`, means 10.119378 (control) and 10.058954 (DCM), log2FC −0.060424, adjusted $p = 0.960652$.\n\nThe `AnnotationDbi::select()` call reported one-to-many probe mappings; these were retained and categorized as ambiguous in the probe-level output. No samples were excluded.\n\nThe notebook records the code, results, and `sessionInfo()` (including limma 3.66.0). It and the CSV deliverables are saved and published:\n\n- [GSE5406 analysis notebook](/home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/notebooks/GSE5406_analysis.ipynb)\n- [Complete probe-level results](/home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/results/tables/GSE5406_limma_probe_level_all.csv)\n- [Selected gene-symbol results](/home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/results/tables/GSE5406_limma_gene_symbol_selected.csv)\n- [Significant probe-level results](/home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/results/tables/GSE5406_limma_probe_level_significant.csv)\n- [Significant gene-symbol results](/home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/results/tables/GSE5406_limma_gene_symbol_significant.csv)\n- [Result summary](/home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/results/tables/GSE5406_limma_summary.csv)\n\nI stopped after Stage 3. No GSE42955 analysis was started.","date":"2026-11-24T06:47:27.288Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/chat/dcm_agent.chat","acp_log_key":"ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc:f915e35c-5358-4033-92b6-b8a48a095ab8","acp_log_subject":"project.e3d18cfc-e2eb-46b5-9a2e-8cb41df2e6b8.acp-log.ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc.f915e35c-5358-4033-92b6-b8a48a095ab8","acp_started_at_ms":1795502615276,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/chat","acp_account_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","acp_runtime_kind":"codex","message_id":"f915e35c-5358-4033-92b6-b8a48a095ab8","thread_id":"ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc","parent_message_id":"3908dc9d-47ec-47c1-80de-ffcb01dc40d4","acp_thread_id":"01a20c06-79b7-78a3-8b91-8c2a6fe6b5a3","acp_usage":{"input_tokens":53351,"cached_input_tokens":46952,"output_tokens":1268,"reasoning_output_tokens":516,"total_tokens":54619,"model_context_window":121600},"acp_manager_finished":true,"acp_active_descendant_thread_ids":[],"acp_active_descendant_agents":0,"acp_subagent_limit_exceeded":false,"acp_background_terminal_processes":0,"acp_ai_usage_may_continue":false}
{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-24T07:05:06.898Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"### 1. Sample metadata and group assignment\n\nThis cell reads the sample fields from the GEO series matrix and uses `!Sample_characteristics_ch1` as the source for group labels. It assigns explicitly labeled idiopathic DCM samples to DCM, unused-donor myocardium samples to non-failing controls, and ischemic cardiomyopathy samples to excluded. Unrecognized labels stay marked for review rather than being guessed.\n\nIt preserves each sample’s GSM ID, original title and label, assigned group, inclusion status, and decision reason in `GSE5406_sample_info.csv`. That manifest makes the sample-selection decisions auditable.\n\n### 2. Limma model and probe-to-gene mapping\n\nThis cell removes the 68 GPL96 control probes identified by the `AFFX` prefix, then maps the remaining probe IDs using `hgu133a.db`. It keeps all probes in the probe-level results, labeling mappings as unique, ambiguous, or unmapped; only uniquely mapped probes can be selected for the gene-symbol table.\n\nIt sets non-failing controls as the reference and fits limma with disease status only. The resulting `groupDCM` coefficient is DCM minus control. It applies BH adjustment, then selects one probe per gene symbol by adjusted p-value, absolute logFC, and probe ID. Finally, it writes the full and significant probe-level and gene-symbol tables.","date":"2026-11-24T07:05:16.654Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/chat/dcm_agent.chat","acp_log_key":"ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc:521c1291-9c43-425f-b40a-3eb33548e89b","acp_log_subject":"project.e3d18cfc-e2eb-46b5-9a2e-8cb41df2e6b8.acp-log.ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc.521c1291-9c43-425f-b40a-3eb33548e89b","acp_started_at_ms":1795503905751,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/chat","acp_account_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","acp_runtime_kind":"codex","message_id":"521c1291-9c43-425f-b40a-3eb33548e89b","thread_id":"ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc","parent_message_id":"4e26e8b2-e330-4578-9430-140b7b5f35ee","acp_thread_id":"01a20c06-79b7-78a3-8b91-8c2a6fe6b5a3","acp_usage":{"input_tokens":63075,"cached_input_tokens":57472,"output_tokens":655,"reasoning_output_tokens":369,"total_tokens":63730,"model_context_window":121600},"acp_manager_finished":true,"acp_active_descendant_thread_ids":[],"acp_active_descendant_agents":0,"acp_subagent_limit_exceeded":false,"acp_background_terminal_processes":0,"acp_ai_usage_may_continue":false}
{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-24T07:06:18.262Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"You’ve got the main idea. A few details:\n\n- It removes **platform control probes** (68 `AFFX` probes), not control samples; all 102 samples remain.\n- Limma models disease status only, with controls as reference, so logFC is **DCM minus control**.\n- The probe-level results keep every tested probe, including ambiguous or unmapped ones. The gene-symbol table selects one probe only for uniquely mapped symbols; ties break by larger absolute logFC, then probe ID.\n- Significance uses BH adjusted $p < 0.05$, with no fold-change cutoff.","date":"2026-11-24T07:06:20.951Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/chat/dcm_agent.chat","acp_log_key":"ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc:0dc75830-9c42-4419-b6d5-ab7751f1cfc1","acp_log_subject":"project.e3d18cfc-e2eb-46b5-9a2e-8cb41df2e6b8.acp-log.ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc.0dc75830-9c42-4419-b6d5-ab7751f1cfc1","acp_started_at_ms":1795503977778,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/chat","acp_account_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","acp_runtime_kind":"codex","message_id":"0dc75830-9c42-4419-b6d5-ab7751f1cfc1","thread_id":"ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc","parent_message_id":"45576f96-82e6-4b72-9d6e-639395e8d9d1","acp_thread_id":"01a20c06-79b7-78a3-8b91-8c2a6fe6b5a3","acp_usage":{"input_tokens":66552,"cached_input_tokens":63072,"output_tokens":281,"reasoning_output_tokens":152,"total_tokens":66833,"model_context_window":121600},"acp_manager_finished":true,"acp_active_descendant_thread_ids":[],"acp_active_descendant_agents":0,"acp_subagent_limit_exceeded":false,"acp_background_terminal_processes":0,"acp_ai_usage_may_continue":false}
{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-24T07:12:15.353Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"I count **4 code cells** that could use tidyverse restyling: metadata/manifest (index 3), validation (5), QC (9), and limma result tables (13). Matrix calculations and the GEO streaming parser can stay in base R.\n\nI count **1 cell** needing clearer comments: validation (index 5), where one opening comment covers several checks and saving the summary. For example, add a short comment before the platform and processing checks.\n\nA tidyverse example: in cell 13, the base R `order()` and `duplicated()` steps for selecting one probe per gene could use `arrange()` and `distinct()`. I made no changes.","date":"2026-11-24T07:12:45.759Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/chat/dcm_agent.chat","acp_log_key":"ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc:93ae3d2f-b42b-464a-b9e5-2f53f7506dd8","acp_log_subject":"project.e3d18cfc-e2eb-46b5-9a2e-8cb41df2e6b8.acp-log.ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc.93ae3d2f-b42b-464a-b9e5-2f53f7506dd8","acp_started_at_ms":1795504334152,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/chat","acp_account_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","acp_runtime_kind":"codex","message_id":"93ae3d2f-b42b-464a-b9e5-2f53f7506dd8","thread_id":"ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc","parent_message_id":"0664f3be-6635-4177-826a-5c842058a71e","acp_thread_id":"01a20c06-79b7-78a3-8b91-8c2a6fe6b5a3","acp_usage":{"input_tokens":80009,"cached_input_tokens":79216,"output_tokens":1922,"reasoning_output_tokens":1777,"total_tokens":81931,"model_context_window":121600},"acp_manager_finished":true,"acp_active_descendant_thread_ids":[],"acp_active_descendant_agents":0,"acp_subagent_limit_exceeded":false,"acp_background_terminal_processes":0,"acp_ai_usage_may_continue":false}
