{"event":"chat-thread-config","sender_id":"__thread_config__:ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc","date":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","thread_id":"ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc","updated_at":"2026-11-24T08:15:57.511Z","updated_by":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","schema_version":2,"name":"DCM Analysis","acp_config":{"model":"gpt-6-luna","sessionMode":"full-access","reasoning":"medium","serviceTier":"standard","paymentSource":"auto","workingDirectory":"/home/user/biom5350/biom5350-dcm-consensus/chat","allowWrite":true,"sessionId":"01a20c06-79b7-78a3-8b91-8c2a6fe6b5a3"},"agent_kind":"acp","agent_model":"gpt-6-luna","agent_mode":"interactive","agent_session_generation":"","acp_goal":{"sessionId":"01a20c06-79b7-78a3-8b91-8c2a6fe6b5a3","observedAt":1795508157511,"goal":null}}
{"event":"chat-thread-state","sender_id":"__thread_state__:ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc","date":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","thread_id":"ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc","state":"complete","active_message_id":"6d301834-35b2-440f-86a3-e652c83a9d77","context_fence":1,"updated_at":"2026-11-24T08:15:57.646Z","schema_version":2}
{"sender_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","event":"chat","schema_version":2,"history":[{"author_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","content":"1. Save the complete probe-level limma table, plus the selected gene-symbol table and significant subsets. This makes it easier to check the results.\n2. Yes, use the larger absolute log2FC to break ties, then the lexically first probe ID.\n\nPlease draft the full analysis plan now and show it to me for review before making any changes or running analyses. Do not create files yet.","date":"2026-11-24T05:48:57.552Z"}],"date":"2026-11-24T05:48:57.552Z","message_id":"f242d648-3e65-4c5d-ac0e-705e839173d1","thread_id":"ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc","parent_message_id":"6067da3d-ac10-40e1-bbc8-0b5732e3c66b","editing":{},"acp_state":"running"}
{"sender_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","event":"chat","schema_version":2,"history":[{"author_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","content":"For GSE42955, what does RMA normalization assume about the arrays, and is that reasonable for 17 heart samples? Also, do we have both before and after normalization plots? Keep it short.","date":"2026-11-24T08:01:57.417Z"}],"date":"2026-11-24T08:01:57.417Z","message_id":"a03070fb-8596-4de9-addb-a00d08a164a8","thread_id":"ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc","parent_message_id":"67a9fdfd-6b26-46a8-916c-14f51b05a6cf","editing":{},"acp_state":"running"}
{"sender_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","event":"chat","schema_version":2,"history":[{"author_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","content":"Here are my decisions:\n\n1. Use only explicitly labeled DCM and non-failing control samples. Exclude ischemic samples.\n2. Use disease status only for the limma model, since there are no usable covariates.\n3. Keep the most significant probe per gene symbol based on adjusted p-value, and document this rule.\n4. Use Jupyter notebooks with an R kernel.\n5. Include sample-level QC, PCA/MDS, and clustering.\n6. Yes, check the available GEO processed files first. I prefer processed matrices for both studies if they are suitable, since GSE5406 has no raw CEL files.\n7. Define consensus genes as adjusted p < 0.05 in both studies with the same direction of log2FC.\n\nPlease continue the interview and cover any remaining decisions from the 12 areas before writing the plan. Do not download expression data or run analyses yet.","date":"2026-11-24T05:34:30.074Z"}],"date":"2026-11-24T05:34:30.074Z","message_id":"8c7d6809-2c63-4d60-8ca6-3fb7c869e062","thread_id":"ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc","parent_message_id":"9dbd33db-6c85-458b-a2f5-bd16272b7bbd","editing":{},"acp_state":"running"}
{"sender_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","event":"chat","schema_version":2,"history":[{"author_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","content":"Here are my remaining decisions:\n\n1. Use the processed matrix if the platform, sample labels, normalization, and log2 scale can be verified. If validation fails, pause and ask me before trying another approach.\n2. Remove platform control probes and keep annotated biological probes. We can decide on any additional filtering after checking the data.\n3. Keep ambiguous or unmapped probes in the probe-level results, but exclude them from the gene-symbol consensus list.\n4. Flag possible sample outliers using QC plots, but don't exclude any sample without my approval.\n5. Use BH-adjusted p < 0.05 with no additional log2FC cutoff. The direction must agree across both studies.\n6. Save results as CSV tables, QC plots as PNG or PDF, and include sessionInfo() in each notebook. Also create a separate consensus notebook.\n\nPlease check that all 12 decision areas have been covered. If anything is missing, ask me before writing the plan. Do not make further GEO requests, download data, run analyses, or modify files until I approve the plan.","date":"2026-11-24T05:38:51.112Z"}],"date":"2026-11-24T05:38:51.112Z","message_id":"34858d2a-05ba-4237-b842-027363c84f36","thread_id":"ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc","parent_message_id":"edb821b5-70d8-4106-b8fb-48bbb72f3d55","editing":{},"acp_state":"running"}
{"sender_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","event":"chat","schema_version":2,"history":[{"author_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","content":"I approve the analysis plan. Please add a note that PCA/MDS should handle missing values and zero-variance features appropriately.\n\nSave the approved plan as `plan/analysis_plan.md` and commit it to Git.\n\nFor now, do not download expression data or run any analysis. Stop after saving and committing the plan, and show me the commit result.","date":"2026-11-24T05:50:25.649Z"}],"date":"2026-11-24T05:50:25.649Z","message_id":"b899bf72-cd40-4420-a4e0-93ffaacd3efb","thread_id":"ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc","parent_message_id":"e5c47a0e-755e-49ef-9683-e40994583af0","editing":{},"acp_state":"running"}
{"sender_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","event":"chat","schema_version":2,"history":[{"author_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","content":"I reviewed Stage 1 and the sample counts match my prediction. You may proceed with Stage 2 for GSE5406 only.\n\nPlease confirm the log2 expression scale and report the actual value range. Generate the planned QC figures, including expression distributions, PCA/MDS, and sample clustering.\n\nCheck for missing values, non-finite values, and zero-variance features as specified in the plan. Flag any possible sample outliers, but do not exclude samples without my approval.\n\nSave the QC figures and document the steps in the GSE5406 R notebook. Show me the QC results and any concerns, then stop before fitting the limma model. Do not start GSE42955 yet.","date":"2026-11-24T06:33:45.889Z"}],"date":"2026-11-24T06:33:45.889Z","message_id":"d10809cb-6aa1-4f3a-8c81-493ed7ce539a","thread_id":"ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc","parent_message_id":"a18724ba-ddc1-4c3f-8223-fc6fb3badefe","editing":{},"acp_state":"running"}
{"sender_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","event":"chat","schema_version":2,"history":[{"author_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","content":"I reviewed Stage 2. Keep all 102 included samples for now, including the 17 flagged samples, since there is no confirmed technical failure.\n\nPlease proceed with Stage 3 for GSE5406 only, following the approved analysis plan.\n\n1. Identify and remove platform control probes, and report the exact number of features tested.\n2. Fit limma using disease status only, with non-failing controls as the reference and log2FC defined as DCM minus control.\n3. Apply BH adjustment and use adjusted p < 0.05, without an extra fold-change cutoff.\n4. Save the complete probe-level results, gene-symbol-selected results, and significant subsets.\n5. Report the number of significant features and how many have absolute log2FC >= 1.\n6. Report the results for NPPA and NPPB if they are represented on the platform.\n7. Show me the code line that sets the reference group and the top-ranked feature's probe ID, group means, and log2FC so I can check it myself.\n\nDo not exclude any samples, do not start GSE42955, and stop after Stage 3 for my review.","date":"2026-11-24T06:43:33.721Z"}],"date":"2026-11-24T06:43:33.721Z","message_id":"3908dc9d-47ec-47c1-80de-ffcb01dc40d4","thread_id":"ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc","parent_message_id":"c35ca684-935c-48f7-b2f4-d713dd09f1af","editing":{},"acp_state":"running"}
{"sender_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","event":"chat","schema_version":2,"history":[{"author_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","content":"I'm working on a project to find genes consistently differentially expressed in DCM compared with non-failing hearts using GSE5406 and GSE42955.\n\nPlease read AGENTS.md first and help me develop an analysis plan in R using limma. I want to compare DCM with controls in each study, exclude ischemic samples, and find genes with adjusted p < 0.05 and the same direction of expression change in both studies.\n\nBefore writing the plan, please interview me about the analysis decisions. Ask questions rather than making assumptions.\n\nFor now, you may read GEO records and sample metadata, but do not download expression data, run analyses, or modify any files until I approve the plan.\n\nThe final deliverables should include the written plan saved as plan/analysis_plan.md, analysis notebooks for both studies, sample information, QC plots, differential expression tables, and a consensus gene list. Use readable R code with short comments and record package versions.\n\nPlease start by asking me the questions needed to make the plan.","date":"2026-11-24T05:27:55.963Z"}],"date":"2026-11-24T05:27:55.963Z","message_id":"cd4d956b-f9c8-4423-8742-44ff0b31b156","thread_id":"ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc","editing":{},"acp_state":"running"}
{"sender_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","event":"chat","schema_version":2,"history":[{"author_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","content":"Let's start Part 3 with GSE5406 only.\n\nPlease follow the approved analysis plan and complete Stage 1 only:\n1. Download the required GSE5406 data.\n2. Build a sample manifest with all 210 samples, including GSM IDs, original labels, assigned groups, inclusion status, and reasons for exclusion.\n3. Check whether we have 86 DCM, 16 non-failing controls, and 108 excluded ischemic samples.\n4. Save the sample manifest in results/tables/ and document the steps in the GSE5406 R notebook.\n\nShow me the actual sample counts, the source of the group labels, and any problems you found.\n\nStop after Stage 1. Do not run QC, fit limma models, or start GSE42955 yet. Wait for my approval before Stage 2.","date":"2026-11-24T06:26:23.552Z"}],"date":"2026-11-24T06:26:23.552Z","message_id":"148270b1-484d-40c0-a09f-7ef6e33b7f34","thread_id":"ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc","parent_message_id":"9f96ad43-9ff1-4d95-aef5-ae8593c125de","editing":{},"acp_state":"running"}
{"sender_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","event":"chat","schema_version":2,"history":[{"author_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","content":"My understanding is that the limma code compares DCM with controls, removes control probes, and keeps the most significant probe for each gene. What did I get wrong or leave out? Keep it short.","date":"2026-11-24T07:06:15.840Z"}],"date":"2026-11-24T07:06:15.840Z","message_id":"45576f96-82e6-4b72-9d6e-639395e8d9d1","thread_id":"ef7005ad-f4b3-4c83-a4ba-a5b43fa8b4fc","parent_message_id":"521c1291-9c43-425f-b40a-3eb33548e89b","editing":{},"acp_state":"running"}
